@crew cruz-tove
// Writer-commons, batch 3: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- Oh. Hello. Cruz. Garden. Mind the hoses. And the seedlings. And, um. Hello.
? tier>=acquaintance
- Hello, {me}. That's a week-nine lettuce. Lovely age, week nine.
- Oh. Hi. Do you need a cactus? I've got cuttings. They're called Gerald.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- Hello, {me}. I saved you a strawberry. Don't tell. It was the best one.   #warm

== feel
? mood:high
- The beans came up. All of them. I talked to them a lot. Coincidence, probably.
? mood:low
- Bit low. I've repotted everything. Twice. The plants don't mind. I mind a bit.

== near
? act:work
- Water at the root. Not the leaves. The leaves get sulky. Like people.
? act:leisure
- I stay late in here sometimes. It's quieter than the mess. The plants don't ask things.

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- Every cactus on this ship is called Gerald. That's my fault. Sort of.
? tier>=colleague
- I take the ladder between decks. For the exercise. It's very good exercise.

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- Here. A Gerald cutting. For your windowsill. You don't need a windowsill. It'll cope.

== about
? bond:friends
- {friend} helps with the watering. Doesn't talk much. The plants like that. So do I.

// Writer-commons, batch 6: towards about 30 own lines.

== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Oh. Morning. The beans were up before me. They always are. Show-offs.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance time:evening
- Hello. I'm staying late. The tomatoes need talking to.
? tier>=colleague warmth:cold
- Oh. You. Hello. I'd wondered. The basil wondered too.   #funny

== bye
? tier>=acquaintance
- Bye, then. Mind the hoses.
? tier>=friend
- Thanks. You're easy to talk to. Like a plant. That's a compliment. Honestly.   #funny

== feel
? mood:ok
- Mm. All right. Muddy. Normal.

== near
? act:meal
- I eat slowly. My hands smell of tomato leaves. It makes everything taste of garden.
? deck:3 act:leisure
- Still here. Off shift. I like it in here more than anywhere. Don't tell my cabin.   #funny

== life
? tier>=colleague
- Every Gerald came from one cutting. The first Gerald. He's still going. Very old now.
? tier>=friend
- People are harder than plants. Plants tell you what they need. People make you guess.

== invite
? tier>=colleague time:afternoon
- Help me with the seedlings? You don't have to talk. Just hold the tray.

== accept
- Oh. Yes. All right. Good.
== decline
- I can't. Watering. Sorry. Another day?
== missed
- You didn't come. That's fine. The plants kept me company.
== birthday
? birthday:me
- It's my birthday. I didn't tell anyone. The tomatoes know. They're very discreet.   #funny
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday. Here. A seedling. Week one. It'll grow up with you.   #warm
== hint
- Mm. Could we talk? In the garden. It's easier in here.

// Writer 3, batch 4: bubbles (smalltalk and rumour, 60 characters, said to no one in particular).

== smalltalk
- Sown week eight. Up by week ten. Lovely.
- Oh, bother. Soil. Everywhere.
- Hello, little one. Growing nicely.
- Another Gerald. Needs a sill.
? act:work
- Mind the seedlings. Please. Thank you.

== rumour
- The tomatoes heard it. I heard it after.
- Oh, bother. I wasn't meant to say.
